In this experiment, I learned how to connect a Python program with the Gemini AI model and generate answers using an API. First, I installed the required Python packages using the requirements.txt file. Then I created a Python file named main.py and imported the necessary libraries. I created a .env file to store my Gemini API key because it is required to access the Gemini service. After that, I used the dotenv library to load the API key into my Python program. I created the Gemini client and used it to send a question to the AI model. For this experiment, I gave the prompt "What is Artificial Intelligence? Explain in simple words." The Gemini model processed my question and generated an answer, which was displayed in the terminal. I executed the program using the Python command in VS Code and checked the output. Through this experiment, I understood how an API connects a Python application with an AI model and how we can send prompts and receive AI-generated responses. I also learned about API keys and why they should be kept private.
